%!PS
% SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 EfterScript contributors
% SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
% expect-output: false
% expect-output: true
% expect-output: 1
% expect-output: undefined
% expect-output: cexec
% Scenario: cexec is not an operator. It is a printer extension that runs
% native code for a particular printer's own processor; PLRM3 has no such
% operator, so the name is undefined and executing it raises `undefined`.
% A driver probes for it exactly this way — inside a guard, with the code
% string pushed first — and relies on the error to leave the guard's own
% result on the stack and the string for it to discard. Defining cexec as
% exec instead would leave the string behind and break the operator that
% follows the probe.
% Expect: false, true, 1, undefined, cexec.
systemdict /cexec known =
{ (native code) cexec } stopped =
count =
$error /errorname get 16 string cvs =
$error /command get 16 string cvs =
